WEBVTT

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.770
Now, at last, it's the final game of the season.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:12.950
The Bats and the Falcons each have three wins, and the deciding match is underway!

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.080
Foul!

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.170
<i>It can't be that he...</i>

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.050
<i>made a foul on purpose.</i>

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.340
<i>Don't you understand yet?</i>

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.630
<i>You can't bring me down...</i>

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.500
<i>with this kind of pitch!</i>

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.010
Out!

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.220
Nice catch!

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.050
Yeah...

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.590
You almost had him.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:10.590
No.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.620
Not at all.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:18.050
<i>It's true that...</i>

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.460
<i>he made a good catch,</i>

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.540
<i>but...</i>

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.520
<i>he didn't use </i>that<i> pitch.</i>

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.280
<i>After all, he focused on his control.</i>

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.990
<i>It was a 90 mph low and outside pitch.</i>

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:33.030
<i>That's not the pitch I came back to hit.</i>

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.340
<i>The ball that I swung at and missed...</i>

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.900
<i>That 100 mph pitch...</i>

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.070
<i>Use that and duel me again, Honda Jr!</i>

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.890
He did it! No outs and a runner on base!

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.060
Okay!

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:30.140
Now hitting, number 56: Goro Shigeno!

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.270
All right!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.570
This is our chance!

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.440
We're counting on you, Shigeno!

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.500
<i>Just take this one point at a time.</i>

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.070
<i>What!?</i>

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.820
<i>A sacrifice bunt...</i>

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.990
<i>And here I was planning to tie it up with a big hit...</i>

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.450
<i>I guess I have no choice.</i>

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.480
Foul!

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.840
That was close!

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:04.880
Boss!

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.810
Shigeno hit a home run earlier, he's a good batter.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.710
Since he might fail anyway, maybe it would be more interesting to just let him hit.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:14.440
Wha-

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.360
D-Don't be stupid!

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.360
Ball!

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.680
If I let him go for a hit, there will be an even <i>bigger</i> chance he'll fail!

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:21.550
Boss!

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.810
I think he should go for a hit too.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:29.770
Rather than speculate, I think we should just count on his fighting spirit right now.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:35.670
The Bats have come this far in the season thanks to Shigeno.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.380
Whatever happens,

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.590
we'll sink or float together with him!

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:44.510
Foul!

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:51.660
<i>This is bad! To be honest, bunting is what I'm worst at!</i>

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.980
<i>I guess it'll be three bunts after all...</i>

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.490
<i>Hit, Shigeno!</i>

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.540
<i>Thanks,</i>

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:21.750
<i>Boss!</i>

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:26.250
He did it!

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.180
It went through!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.590
Go around!

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:33.990
Safe.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:34.890
Safe!

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.560
You did it!

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.420
A well-timed double!

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.730
Just a one point difference!

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.140
Well done, Shigeno!

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.610
Nice batting!

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:48.570
<i>Geez, what a guy!</i>

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.120
<i>Mr. Honda,</i>

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.690
<i>it seems like there really...</i>

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:57.580
<i>is something extraordinary about your son.</i>

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.750
Now hitting, number 2: Kelloge!

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.990
Okay! Go for it, Kelloge!

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.420
Keep this going!

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.940
<i>Just one more point.</i>

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.590
<i>At least hit it to right field...</i>

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.220
<i>and let the runner proceed!</i>

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.110
He's going for it!

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:27.360
Ball!

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.700
Safe!

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:39.120
That was too reckless!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.160
But now there's a runner on third, with no outs.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:42.700
What a great chance!

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.630
Even if it's a pop fly, we can tie it up!

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:50.430
Unbelievable.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.150
Did you miss a sign?

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.790
Miss a sign?

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:55.760
No.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:59.830
I stole because I was 100% sure I'd succeed.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:00.980
What?

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:03.460
Since the runner is a pitcher,

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.620
the battery wasn't too concerned.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:08.400
That pitcher isn't good at making quick throws,

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.290
and on top of that,

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.450
I knew from how he was holding the ball that he'd throw a change-up.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.680
Ball!

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:20.960
Ball two!

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.130
Damn it!

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.050
Pitcher change!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:32.010
Attention, please, now pitching, number 19: Browny!

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.560
Hey, Honda Jr.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.260
Since we've got nothing to do, let me show you something.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.410
Look at the second floor of the box seats.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:54.660
Your archenemy,

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:55.990
who killed your father,

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.450
has shown up.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.210
Gibson!

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:03.640
Not for me...

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:06.120
He's here to see you, he said.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:09.670
Oh man, I really don't know what he's thinking.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:15.000
To be so interested in the son of the guy he killed so many years ago...

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.570
No matter what he does,

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:21.230
there's no way you could forgive him for killing your father, right?

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.710
It's just for him to feel better about himself.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.640
Hey, you...

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:29.950
He's your own father, how can you talk about him like that?

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:36.230
Also, I'm not sure where you got that idea,

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.940
but I don't hate Gibson at all.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:43.210
And of course, I didn't come to America to take revenge.

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:47.460
Gibson is...

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:50.500
the only one in the world who can...

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.720
be the replacement...

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.260
for my dad, whom I never got the chance to surpass.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:03.640
I admire him. He's a great man that I won't stop pursuing.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.710
He came all the way here to watch this game.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:15.740
Let's both show him our best performance until it's over!

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:20.240
Play!

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:22.700
<i>Why?</i>

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:27.250
<i>Why doesn't he hate my father?</i>

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:30.380
<i>I wanted to surpass my father too,</i>

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.420
<i>so I continued with baseball,</i>

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.460
<i>but that...</i>

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:36.380
<i>wasn't because of admiration or respect.</i>

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.640
<i>I needed to take vengeance...</i>

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.850
<i>upon my father, who never showed any love to his family.</i>

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:45.980
<i>By becoming better than him at baseball,</i>

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.510
<i>I intended to settle our past.</i>

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:50.770
<i>But despite that,</i>

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.480
<i>why is he...?</i>

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.860
Second!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.450
Leave it to me!

00:09:58.660 --> 00:09:59.570
Get down!

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:02.450
Out!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.240
Back home!

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.460
He touched up!

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.500
Why, you!

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.300
Safe! Safe!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.720
All right!

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.610
The Bats have tied it!

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:23.290
The runner, Shigeno, touched up nicely!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.290
Nice going, Goro!

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:27.700
Will the Memphis Bats be able to make this great turn of events into a comeback?

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.600
Good work!

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:29.210
You can win this!

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:32.040
You did it!

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.270
<i>He's different than me.</i>

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.940
<i>His motivation for coming here...</i>

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.740
<i>is different than mine.</i>

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.860
<i>He loves baseball from the bottom of his heart!</i>

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.470
<i>Also,</i>

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:45.240
<i>he's genuinely having fun playing baseball!</i>

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:51.080
This is a free fansub.

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:51.080
Not for sale or rent.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:58.970
<i>Junior.</i>

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.890
<i>Have you started to grasp something from Goro's play?</i>

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.260
<i>He loves baseball from the bottom of his heart...</i>

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:10.390
<i>and has come this far by playing his best in every game.</i>

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:13.020
<i>He's fundamentally different than you,</i>

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.460
<i>in that you're fueled by your grudge toward me,</i>

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.740
<i>and that you use baseball as a means of revenge.</i>

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.010
<i>If you don't realize that,</i>

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.700
<i>you won't be able to hit Goro's pitch!</i>

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.020
Strike!

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.420
<i>Why?</i>

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.610
<i>When his father was killed in baseball,</i>

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:33.130
<i>how can he have fun playing this sport!?</i>

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:37.380
<i>My father too?</i>

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.670
<i>Does my father feel the same way?</i>

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:42.770
<i>Until now,</i>

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:45.610
<i>I thought my dad had always been concerned about him...</i>

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:48.920
<i>because he carried the cross of having killed Honda Shigeharu.</i>

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:52.140
<i>But maybe that's not it.</i>

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:56.270
<i>Maybe,</i>

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:58.530
<i>because my old man also loves baseball...</i>

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:00.340
<i>and has fun playing it,</i>

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:04.620
<i>he's interested in that guy because they have the same feelings and the same soul.</i>

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:08.910
<i>Do they both see something that I can't see?</i>

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:14.270
<i>Something that I have never been able to see?</i>

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:17.170
<i>I'll say it again:</i>

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.810
<i>You're not good enough to hit Goro's pitches yet.</i>

00:12:19.810 --> 00:12:21.510
<i>Not physically,</i>

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:23.380
<i>and not mentally.</i>

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:27.790
<i>Is the problem that I'm not enjoying baseball?</i>

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:29.840
<i>You're telling me that's why I can't hit his pitch!?</i>

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.420
<i>This is a bad joke.</i>

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.860
<i>You've always ignored me.</i>

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:37.840
<i>I don't want to hear that from someone like you.</i>

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.600
<i>Even if he's pitching at 100 mph,</i>

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:45.280
<i>to be struck out without even grazing a single pitch is disgraceful.</i>

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:47.030
<i>Ever since Little League,</i>

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.040
<i>you've been excellent against fastballs when batting in the left batter's box.</i>

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:52.880
<i>That's it!</i>

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.180
<i>That's what it is!</i>

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:59.670
<i>It's true that I've always been better at hitting fastballs from the left.</i>

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:03.430
<i>It can't be, that even though I didn't know,</i>

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.930
<i>my old man was always watching me.</i>

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.160
<i>Even if that's the truth,</i>

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.850
<i>it doesn't matter at this point.</i>

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.530
Strike out!

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:26.540
<i>Left batter's box...</i>

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.830
All right, two outs!

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:41.000
<i>Since I stepped up to bat in the fifth inning,</i>

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.610
<i>I've made no hits.</i>

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:47.760
<i>Gibson has come all the way here to watch, after all.</i>

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:50.100
<i>I'll be sure to continue like this!</i>

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:56.190
Now hitting, number 1: Joe Gibson Jr!

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:59.160
Do your best, Shigeno-kun!

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.260
This is a critical situation.

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:04.490
Suppress him, somehow!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.570
What!?

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:10.570
What!?

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:12.520
L-Left batter's box!?

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.000
L-Left batter's box!?

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:21.360
<i>It's not like my grudge toward my father is gone.</i>

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:25.950
<i>I'm hitting from the left to ensure that I give my best performance!</i>

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:27.660
<i>Now,</i>

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:28.880
<i>pitch!</i>

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.550
<i>Pitch that 100 mph one at me!</i>

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.330
<i>So you've realized it, Junior.</i>

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:37.020
<i>The difference between your baseball playing and Goro's.</i>

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:39.790
What's he doing?

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:44.550
Mr. Gibson, why did he choose the left batter's box when he's batting against a left-handed pitcher?

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:48.320
He was, by nature, a left-handed batter.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:52.310
He couldn't deal with southpaws' breaking balls in high school,

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:53.850
so he became a switch hitter.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:59.180
But, when matched against Shigeno, who doesn't throw breaking balls,

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:03.340
he'll be able to do better by batting from his preferred side.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:08.510
<i>This is the first time you've listened to what I've said, Junior.</i>

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:10.720
Hey, be careful!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:14.870
He's definitely got something up his sleeve by going left against left.

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:18.080
It's not "something."

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:23.920
Right now, he's genuinely trying to challenge me.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.320
With Gibson watching me,

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.370
this battle...

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.490
I can't afford to lose it!

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.510
<i>Junior.</i>

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:36.720
<i>You've come back to the Minors only to get revenge on Goro.</i>

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:38.840
<i>If your feelings of frustration...</i>

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:40.960
<i>and recklessness are genuine,</i>

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.830
<i>then no matter how this goes,</i>

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.380
<i>this first true rival you've faced...</i>

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:51.550
<i>will surely improve you by one or two steps.</i>

00:15:55.680 --> 00:16:00.430
<i>Though my rival will disappear in just one game.</i>

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:04.690
Ball!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:09.900
Okay!

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.480
Be careful!

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:13.320
Ball!

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.230
Ball two!

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:16.380
<i>That's good.</i>

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:19.120
<i>Stay away from a reckless duel with this guy.</i>

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:20.650
<i>Damn!</i>

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.080
<i>Why?</i>

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:26.380
<i>I can't throw that 100 mph pitch that I threw when the bases were loaded!</i>

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:32.260
<i>He's giving me all he's got.</i>

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:35.220
<i>If I throw the same pitches,</i>

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.180
<i>he'll definitely hit them this time!</i>

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:41.020
<i>Gibson has come all the way to watch,</i>

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:44.350
<i>so why can't I pitch it!?</i>

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:46.190
Ball!

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:47.680
Ball three!

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.460
<i>He's clearly overexerting himself.</i>

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:56.740
Don't run away!

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.990
Why aren't you throwing that 100 mph pitch?

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.870
Fight me, Honda Jr!

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:04.330
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:08.670
<i>I know that, you bastard!</i>

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.250
<i>So high!</i>

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:12.550
<i>I won't take...</i>

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:14.520
<i>a walk!</i>

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.350
Oh, no!

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.530
Short!

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:29.730
Damn!

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:33.650
Back home!

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:43.120
Safe!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.390
Inside-the-park home run!

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:49.210
It's 3-2!

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.350
I misjudged you.

00:17:56.430 --> 00:18:00.720
Since you made me hit a ball, it didn't cross the fence, but...

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:04.270
why didn't you throw that 100 mph pitch down the middle!?

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:11.980
To have thought of a coward like you as my rival makes me look stupid.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:15.230
Sorry, Shigeno.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.990
You pitched well by trying to walk him.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.800
I should have made sure he couldn't hit it.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.130
Don't be stupid.

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:27.360
I wasn't trying to walk him.

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:32.350
I tried to throw that 100 mph pitch,

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:33.710
but you saw how it turned out.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:40.760
Out!

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:46.050
It's the bottom of the 8th, and the Falcons have gained a precious point.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:49.850
The Triple A finals are finally at their climax!

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:52.980
Can the Falcons hold on to this?

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:55.210
On the mound, the Falcons' trump card,

00:18:55.210 --> 00:18:57.400
the closer, Wilkins, has appeared!

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:03.230
Not yet!

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.470
The game isn't over yet!

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.910
One point is no big deal.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:11.220
Strike out!

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:12.380
Damn it!

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:13.790
Yes!

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:19.090
<i>They managed to take a point from me that I couldn't afford to give!</i>

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:21.210
<i>Like Sanders said,</i>

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:23.470
<i>I should have just walked him.</i>

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:26.060
<i>I haven't managed to pitch 100 mph since that game,</i>

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.530
<i>but I still ignored our situation in this game,</i>

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:33.480
<i>got mad since I'm up against Junior, and threw a half-assed pitch.</i>

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:38.780
Strike out!

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:41.260
Two outs...

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:46.490
Now hitting, number 8: Sanders!

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:52.780
<i>Why did I intentionally stay in the Minor League Championship?</i>

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.650
<i>It was to help Alice, who took me under her wing;</i>

00:19:56.650 --> 00:20:00.800
<i>and the boss and coach, who patiently used me as a closer;</i>

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.040
<i>and for my teammates, who've helped me improve;</i>

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:06.680
<i>and for Sanders.</i>

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.330
<i>I wanted to wear this uniform and help us win the championship, but...</i>

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:15.650
Strike two!

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:19.380
Dear...

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:20.380
Papa!

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:21.650
Do your best!

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:27.580
<i>Shigeno is the one who's brought the Bats this far, there's no doubt!</i>

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:29.450
<i>He focused on winning,</i>

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:32.250
<i>and kept inspiring the team.</i>

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:37.590
<i>He convinced me not to retire, after showing me my son's feelings.</i>

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:43.300
<i>That I can be here today is all his doing.</i>

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.970
<i>I can't let Shigeno end up as...</i>

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:49.060
<i>a losing pitcher...</i>

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.600
<i>in this last game!</i>

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:14.730
It's out of here!

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.880
We're tied!

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:19.550
Well done, Sanders!

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:21.630
I did it!

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:23.340
Dear...

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:25.180
Papa is the best!

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:30.600
Sergeant!

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.680
You did it!

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.660
Stop it!

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:36.100
Not the beard! It hurts!

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:38.400
You bastard!

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:39.560
Damn, that hurts!

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:40.500
Old man.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:43.710
Shigeno!

00:21:45.100 --> 00:21:46.610
I'm in awe.

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:50.030
It's ten years too early for you to retire.

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:13.720
Now hitting, number 4: Shelby!

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:15.100
Play!

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:17.520
<i>Thanks, old man.</i>

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:20.010
<i>With your great hit,</i>

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:21.850
<i>as long as I don't screw up,</i>

00:22:21.850 --> 00:22:24.190
<i>we won't lose this match!</i>

00:22:28.190 --> 00:22:29.870
<i>Come, Shigeno!</i>

00:22:30.370 --> 00:22:31.280
<i>Here I go!</i>

00:24:12.140 --> 00:24:14.050
The final game, with the
championship on the line...

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:15.300
is finally at its climax!

00:24:15.830 --> 00:24:17.930
You're on, Gibson Jr!

00:24:18.370 --> 00:24:20.810
I'll show you the baseball spirit...

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.470
I inherited from my dad!

00:24:23.400 --> 00:24:24.650
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:26.070
Oath.

00:24:26.070 --> 00:24:28.480
Run towards the stage of your dreams!
